This file keeps web/dist present in a fresh clone.

package web embeds this directory with //go:embed, which is resolved at
compile time and fails if the directory does not exist. The dashboard build
output is not checked in, so without this placeholder `go build ./...` would
fail on a clone that has never run a frontend build — and the Go side is
meant to be workable with no Node toolchain installed at all.

web.Assets() looks for index.html rather than for any file, so a clone
holding only this placeholder reports "no dashboard built" and says how to
build one, instead of serving an empty directory.

Run `make ui` to populate this directory for real.
